  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The acids which contain $\\mathrm{P}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond have strong reducing properties. Thus $\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{PO}_{2}$ acid is good reducing agent as it contains two P-H bonds. For example, it reduces $\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$ to metallic silver.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/9jdPCxj4Th9wFFql8EsIaNkzC-sXhad3i2tPe2Jn5yg.original.fullsize.png\">",
